WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.000
Tow-N-Go branding tops an autumn garage scene with moving boxes, an armchair and a glowing pumpkin. Text asks, “What's haunting your weekend?” followed by “A move. A cleanup. That unfinished project.”

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:12.100
A black enclosed trailer appears on an autumn driveway. Text reads, “Enclosed trailers. Keep your cargo covered. Check cargo dimensions and the trailer's door opening.”

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:20.350
A black dump trailer is shown against a lake and mountain backdrop. Text reads, “Dump trailers. Space isn't payload. Know your material. Check the trailer's load limit.”

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:25.600
A flatdeck trailer carries stacks of lumber. Text reads, “Flatdeck trailers. Know your load. Confirm dimensions and total weight.”

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:31.800
An enclosed trailer stands with its rear ramp lowered. Text reads, “Empty-trailer delivery & collection. We bring the trailer. You load and use it. We collect it as arranged.”

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.800
A pickup is attached to a loaded flatdeck trailer near a lake. Text reads, “Pickup, transport & delivery. You load it. Tow-N-Go hauls it. Transport to your agreed destination.”

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:38.650
A close-up of a dark spider provides a Halloween transition.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:51.000
A black and gold end card with glowing pumpkins reads, “Less haunting. More hauling.” It lists enclosed, dump and flatdeck trailers, 778-215-3422 and towandgotrailers.ca, serving Kelowna, the Okanagan and beyond.
